<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Shortcut Keys</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="103.474%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>You can view and modify all shortcut keys from <span class="Path">System</span><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">&gt; Shortcut Keys</span></i> dialog.</p>
<p class="Normal"><img src="shortcut_keys_files/shortcut_keys.gif" width="637px" height="452px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="Normal">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Show shortcut in menus</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Enable this option to display the shortcut keys in all menus.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Defaults</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Sets all commands to their default shortcuts. User defined shortcuts for commands that do not have shortcut keys by default will be deleted.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Print</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Prints a table of the current shortcut keys via the default printer. The table contains menu location, shortcut key, and description of every command available in KUBE.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Dump</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Saves a table of the current shortcut keys in Rich Text Format (RTF) file. The table contains menu location, shortcut key, and description of every command available in KUBE. The default name of the file is '</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>KUBEVersion</i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Shortcuts.rtf', where</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>KUBEVersion</i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is the full version of KUBE.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OK</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Confirms all shortcut keys changes and closes the dialog.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cancel</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Rejects all shortcut keys changes and closes the dialog.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p>Modifying commands shortcut keys is possible in two ways:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Right-click on the command and a context menu will appear:</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Normal"><img src="shortcut_keys_files/context_menu.gif" width="504px" height="83px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">'Change the shortcut key...'</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select it to add/modify shortcut.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">'Remove shortcut key'</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select it to remove the shortcut assigned to this command.</p>
<ol start="2" type="1" class="whs6">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Double-click on the command to invoke the dialog for adding/modifying shortcut keys.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>If a shortcut exists it will appear next to 'Current key:'</p>
<p><img src="shortcut_keys_files/change_shortcut_key.gif" width="251px" height="147px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p>If it does not exist &lt;none&gt; will appear next to 'Current key:'</p>
<p><img src="shortcut_keys_files/change_shortcut_key_1.gif" width="251px" height="147px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p>Then press the new key combination or press Cancel button or ESC to close this dialog.</p>
<p>The shortcut must be any combination between the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>optional keys</b></span> (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl</b></span> and/or <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift</b></span> and/or <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Alt</b></span>) and a <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>regular key</b></span>. Please note that if you use optional keys they must be pressed first. The sequence of pressing the optional keys is of no importance. Finally the shortcut is always displayed as <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + Shift + Alt +</b></span> ...</p>
<p>The regular keys are: all functional keys (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>F1...F12</b></span>), all keys with printable characters (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>`</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>0..9</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>-</b></span>, =, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A...Z</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>[</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>]</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>;</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>\</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>,</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>/</b></span>), <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Caps Lock</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scroll Lock</b></span>, and all Numeric Pad keys (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>0..9</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>/</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>*</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>-</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>+</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Num Lock</b></span>). The following keys: Insert, Delete, Home, End, Page Up, Page Down, and the four arrow keys, are treated as their equivalents from the Numeric Pad.</p>
<p>The following keys are not used in any shortcut key combination: Spacebar, Enter (both keys), ESC, Tab, Backspace, PrtScr/SysRq, Pause/Break, any other non-standard keys (Windows specific, Power, Sleep, Wake, etc.)</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>If you press some key combination that is already reserved for another command a warning will appear:</p>
<p><img src="shortcut_keys_files/warning.gif" width="443px" height="172px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<p>It shows for which command the shortcut is assigned to. You can replace it (deleting the shortcut to the previous command) or cancel.</p>
